TITLE:: SwarmMath
summary:: Generate and capture additive swarm controls
categories:: Libraries>SwarmSynth

DESCRIPTION::
SwarmMath generates controls for each base frequency, partial and variation.
Captures require no server and contain generated inputs, not measured spectra.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: playbackSnapshot
Capture all controls with the same callback order and random consumption as
code::calc::. The ratio resolves once per event before the other callbacks.

ARGUMENT:: seed
Optional integer random seed; nil uses the current stream.

ARGUMENT:: preserveRandom
Defaults to false. When true, restore the calling thread's random state after
capture, including on errors. Use true for stable previews.

RETURNS::
An array of records with code::index::, code::freqIndex::, zero-based
code::partial:: and code::variation::, code::baseFrequency::, code::ratio::,
and a code::values:: dictionary of generated Synth controls.

DISCUSSION::
Existing code::snapshot(params, seed):: retains its inspection ordering and
random-state preservation. Redrawing a display should reuse captured records.
code::SwarmSynth.setSampled(sampled, fadeTime, excludeParams, createNew)::
accepts cached control pairs. Pass code::createNew: false:: for live updates
that must not recreate missing nodes. Read code::synth.params:: afterward for
merged controls, including retained phase/pan and defaults.

EXAMPLES::
code::
state = SwarmMath([110, 165], 8, 2, [
    freq: { |e| e.freq * e.p1 }, amp: { |e| e.vol / e.p1 }
], 0.1);
preview = state.playbackSnapshot(20261009, true);
// Once playback has been created:
// records = state.playbackSnapshot;
// playback.setSampled(records.collect { |r| r[\values].asPairs });
::
